1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,707
What happens when thousands of people panic at the same time?

2
00:00:03,860 --> 00:00:05,825
Some people react immediately.

3
00:00:05,975 --> 00:00:08,267
Others wait, watching everyone around them.

4
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:12,779
When information is unclear, people often look to others for clues.

5
00:00:12,929 --> 00:00:16,221
One person's reaction can influence the people nearby.

6
00:00:16,371 --> 00:00:18,803
And that reaction can ripple through the crowd.

7
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:22,887
Uncertainty. No one knows what is happening.

8
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:26,416
Social influence. We copy the people around us.

9
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:30,380
And stress. So almost everyone heads for the one exit they know.

10
00:00:30,530 --> 00:00:33,183
Fix one: a slanted barrier in front of the door.

11
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:37,130
In simulations, it splits the push, and the door stops clogging.

12
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:40,288
Fix two: clear announcements send people to every exit.

13
00:00:40,438 --> 00:00:42,332
Smarter exits, calmer crowds.

14
00:00:43,150 --> 00:00:44,981
Follow InvisiTech for more.

